    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Powertrip is Monster Magnet’s fourth studio album and the record that brought the New Jersey band its biggest commercial breakthrough. Released in 1998 on A&M Records, it sharpened the group’s heavy stoner-rock sound into a more direct, hook-driven form, powered by Dave Wyndorf’s swaggering vocals, thick guitar riffs, and a space-age, hard-rocking sense of spectacle. The album’s best-known single, “Space Lord,” became a mainstream hit and helped push Powertrip onto the Billboard 200, where it reached No. 97, while also earning gold certification in the U.S.\n\nMusically, the album blends hard rock, stoner rock, and heavy metal influences with a polished but still muscular production style, making it more accessible than Monster Magnet’s earlier, more psychedelic work. Songs like “Powertrip,” “Temple of Your Dreams,” and “See You in Hell” underline its larger-than-life approach, and the record is widely regarded as one of the band’s defining releases. Its strong reception cemented Monster Magnet’s reputation as one of the key rock acts of the late 1990s alternative-heavy scene.",
